 "scope": "curve25519-sparse-elimination-v1",
 "statement": "Fixed producer qualification of a new bounded ordinary sparse Buchberger/partial-root-extraction baseline with dynamic sparse monomials and exact BigUint coefficients. On the declared actual-field q1/k2 arity2 known-answer control, the public-System-only solver returns71 original values satisfying81 equations and independent indexed-row/group replay as positive columns(j1,t0),(j2,t0). That case uses8 branch nodes and zero Buchberger calls; its root comes from linear/quadratic propagation, not an observed Groebner advantage. Eleven fixed polynomial/interface cases,106 unchanged-sqrt comparisons, nine forced resource refusals, malformed/canonicalization and root mutation/truncation controls pass. The1100-variable test has only one constrained variable. A work1 refusal on the immutable1059-variable input is admission-only, not a full solve attempt. Six compiled-in pins/composite49 inputs/archive round-trips match; focused release test/fmt/strict Clippy pass. Counters are partial primitive/reservation data, not normalized complete cold cost, peak RSS or a performance/exponent result. No absence certificate, new general theorem, novel algorithm or signed standing is established."
